+IMPLEMENTER_REPORT:
+
+ROUND: 1
+
+STATUS: DONE
+
+SUGGESTION_RESOLUTIONS:
+- Suggestion S1 (retire the entry-level `resolution` field): implemented. `ExpectedSetEntry` no longer carries a directory-level verdict; `ResolutionStatus` now documents a single `SkillFile` and its missing reason. Consumers already derived failure from files, so only the struct definition, the `generate_manifest` predicate, and one synthetic test fixture needed to change.
+- Suggestion S2 (make `generate_manifest` read file-level failure): implemented. It now calls `skill.is_failed()` instead of matching an entry-level status, which is the same predicate `dev` already uses.
+
+CLAUSE CHECKS:
+- I01: New behavior code (`generate_manifest` predicate) was covered by a failing test first: `generate_manifest_skips_an_entry_with_any_missing_skill_file` failed on the old code (`panic` at `crates/skill-index/src/lib.rs:1069`), then passed after the change. The field removal itself is a compile-enforced deletion with no runtime observable, so no separate test can assert absence.
