+- Baseline note: the first full baseline run showed one failure in the `shared` crate library tests that did not reproduce in three subsequent full runs; `crates/shared` is untouched by this ticket, and I did not adjust it.
+- No test assertions were relaxed: the `Missing { reason }` matches in `missing_vendor_directory_yields_failed_entry` / `missing_upstream_directory_yields_failed_entry` now read the same reason from `skill_file(None).resolution`, and the old entry-level matches were removed.
+
+CHANGED_FILES:
+- `crates/skill-index/src/lib.rs` — removed `ExpectedSetEntry::resolution`; `generate_manifest` now uses `is_failed()`; `ResolutionStatus`/entry docs updated; added `generate_manifest_skips_an_entry_with_any_missing_skill_file`; re-pointed two missing-directory tests at their owned file.
+- `crates/validation-runner/src/lib.rs` — removed the synthetic entry-level `resolution` from the `test_entry` fixture; refreshed failed-entry section and `matrix_case` comments.
